  "notes": "Whether it stays after 2026 not stated. Drawn from April 2026 photos of N1776R (left side). Not the Heart fin: navy, white and red bands on the same lines as the Heart's. The right side is not seen in these photos. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on the April 2026 broadside photo (doors as the scale: 45 px/m): the quotation's two lines had no length and ran far too long; measured, 'Life, Liberty and the' runs 21.9-29.3 m back (x 0.575-0.771) above the windows, 'pursuit of Happiness.' 24.6-31.0 m (0.646-0.816) just under them, the script's lowercase about 0.45 of its capitals. '1776' checked (6.3-12.4 m, as drawn). The red sweep and the cream under it, traced as points along curves, made smooth. The fin's bands put on the Heart fin's lines as re-measured on Colorado One (the white where the Heart's red is, the red where its yellow is), with the same 'Southwest' title; drawn on the 737-8. 2026-11-15: a Commons photo whose source is airliners.net was dropped (the dataset doesn't draw from photo sites); its parts now cite the other photo."
